{"v":1,"agent":"copilot-cli","cli_version":"0.10.3","type":"assistant","ts":"2026-08-31T16:32:00.799Z","id":"d650dbd1-960f-409b-bc31-dfe8982df8c2","content":[{"text":"Now I'll insert the fix right after the appearance-toggle rule, keeping nav-bar related overrides together. ","type":"text"},{"id":"toolu_01TjWXiAEB3KK3JCZ5C6u7hZ","input":"{\"filePath\": \"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/docs/.vitepress/theme/pantoken.css\", \"oldString\": \"/* Keep custom outline social icons from inheriting VitePress's solid icon fill. */\\n.VPSocialLink \u003e svg {\\n  fill: none !important;\\n}\", \"newString\": \"/* Keep custom outline social icons from inheriting VitePress's solid icon fill. */\\n.VPSocialLink \u003e svg {\\n  fill: none !important;\\n}\\n\\n/* VitePress rounds and scrolls `.VPMenu` on the same box; the translations flyout lists 40+ locales,\\n   so its native scrollbar routinely squares off the corners it touches. Move the radius + shadow to\\n   the flyout's outer `.menu` wrapper and clip through `overflow: hidden` there instead, leaving\\n   `.VPMenu` to scroll unconstrained by rounding. */\\n.VPNavBarTranslations .menu {\\n  overflow: hidden;\\n  border-radius: 12px;\\n  box-shadow: var(--vp-shadow-3);\\n}\\n\\n.VPNavBarTranslations .menu .VPMenu {\\n  border-radius: 0;\\n  box-shadow: none;\\n}\\n\\n@media (min-width: 768px) {\\n  .VPNavBarTranslations .menu,\\n  .VPNavBarTranslations .menu .VPMenu {\\n    max-height: 50vh;\\n  }\\n}\"}","name":"replace_string_in_file","result":{"output":"","status":"success"},"type":"tool_use"}]}
{"v":1,"agent":"copilot-cli","cli_version":"0.10.3","type":"assistant","ts":"2026-08-31T16:32:04.032Z","id":"0938ada9-25cf-4de1-930d-34afd76c9bf3","content":[{"text":"Added an override in [pantoken.css](docs/.vitepress/theme/pantoken.css#L242-L262): the outer `.menu` wrapper now owns the rounded corners + shadow via `overflow: hidden`, while the inner `.VPMenu` (which VitePress already makes scrollable) loses its own radius/shadow so the native scrollbar can't square off a corner. On desktop (`≥768px`) both get a `50vh` cap so the language list scrolls instead of overflowing the viewport.\n\nPlease refresh `http://localhost:5173/` and open the language flyout to confirm the rounded corners hold with the scrollbar.","type":"text"}]}
